{"id":"mattaniah","name":"Mattaniah","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:mattaniah"],"types":[],"standing":"single-index","indexes":["nave"],"thin":false,"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Mattaniah","text":"Gift of Jehovah. (1.) A Levite, son of Heman, the chief of the ninth class of temple singers (1 Chr. 25:4, 16). (2.) A Levite who assisted in purifying the temple at the reformation under Hezekiah (2 Chr. 29:13). (3.) The original name of Zedekiah (q.v.), the last of the kings of Judah (2 Kings 24:17). He was the third son of Josiah, who fell at Megiddo. He succeeded his nephew Jehoiakin."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H4983","lemma":"מַתַּנְיָה","xlit":"Mattanyâh","gloss":"Mattanjah, the name of ten Israelites","kjv":"Mattaniah","count":11,"share":1},{"strong":"H1121","lemma":"בֵּן","xlit":"bên","gloss":"a son , in the widest sense , etc.)","kjv":"afflicted, age, ite, ed one","count":8,"share":0.73},{"strong":"H251","lemma":"אָח","xlit":"ʼâch","gloss":"a brother )","kjv":"another, brother; kindred, like, other","count":3,"share":0.27}],"verses":["2Kgs.24.17","1Chr.25.4","1Chr.25.16","2Chr.20.14","2Chr.29.13","Ezra.10.26","Ezra.10.27","Ezra.10.30","Ezra.10.37","Neh.12.8","Neh.13.13"],"witnesses":["n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n","n"],"agreed":0,"broader":[],"narrower":[],"related":[{"id":"zedekiah","type":"seealso","why":"Nave's Topical Bible lists it under See also"},{"id":"jebusites","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.068,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"zechariah-zecharias","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.057,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"asaph","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.044,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"amorites","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.021,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"abdon","type":"lexical","strong":"H1121","why":"both lead with בֵּן (H1121)"},{"id":"accursed","type":"lexical","strong":"H1121","why":"both lea